{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NnghkQLz6sJe47gVaUHZ4U","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Task goal\n2\tIndependently verify four small defect fixes in one commit, 65c37f2 (pre-build base 2c839cf). Tickets: .sdlc/.0259-fanout-gate-preflight, .sdlc/.0260-solo-session-limit-resume, .sdlc/.0262-close-citation-scan-gaps, .sdlc/.0273-codex-selftest-claude-path (read each handoff.md). Each regression test must fail without its fix and pass with it.\n3\t\n4\t## Step 1: Verify the four fixes\n5\tlevel: L3\n6\t\n7\t### Do\n8\t- T-0259 (scripts/fanout.py): an uncommitted handoff refusal now names the force-add of the ignored path; a plan whose start commit tracks package.json and whose gates never install prints a `note:` naming `npm ci`; a red gate in a worktree with package.json and no node_modules appends a hint. Test: fanout selftest case 20. Docs: docs/maintenance/sdlc-internals.md.\n9\t- T-0260 (scripts/run.sh, scripts/solo_run.py): a failed run whose log shows 429 or a session limit writes `<role>-<level>.limit` and prints `run.sh: session limit: resume with: ...` (exit stays 1); solo_run.py writes `solo.limit` and prints a resume hint. Tests: run-selftest.sh case `session limit` and solo_run.py selftest.\n10\t- T-0262 (scripts/tickets.py): `outside_refs` also scans the ticket root with ignore rules off so citations under a gitignored `.sdlc` are found, refused, and rewritable; `--force` prints `left refs to ...`. Test: tickets.py selftest `(u) refs` cases.\n11\t- T-0273 (scripts/codex-selftest.py): `test_fanout_uses_codex` now checks argv (role script, and not the claude CLI) instead of a `claude` substring, so it passes when the repo path contains `claude`. This worktree lives under `.claude/worktrees`, which is the repro.\n12\tTo show red before, work in a throwaway worktree under `$SDLC_TMP_WORKTREES` at HEAD, revert only the non-test hunks of each fix there (the `deps_note` call, the red-gate hint and the force-add wording in fanout.py; the `limit_marker` function body in run.sh and the `limit_hint` call in solo_run.py; the ignore-off scan block in `outside_refs`), run the matching selftest, and say what you did. For T-0273 run the OLD test body from base 2c839cf in this path and note that it fails.\n13\t\n14\t### Acceptance criteria\n15\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/fanout.py selftest`\n16\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/tickets.py selftest`\n17\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/solo_run.py selftest`\n18\t- `bash plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/run-selftest.sh`\n19\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/codex-selftest.py CodexTests.test_fanout_uses_codex`\n20\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/check.py`\n21\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/codex_roles.py generate --check`\n22\t- `python3 scripts/check-packaging.py`\n23\t- Each of the four regression tests goes red with its fix reverted (observed, not read).\n24\t\n25\t## Builder note\n26\tThe builder (Sonnet) saw red then green for each. Treat that as an unverified claim.\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d37f6391-7843-414c-9b5f-3ff80d3a3d36","uuid":"bc495ea4-4565-45fb-8c21-dac7a93edd03","timestamp":"2026-10-05T23:26:41.434Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kimgranlund/Projects/nonoun/sdlc-lite/.claude/worktrees/agent-aaee304bcd5963894/.sdlc/verify-defect-fixes-0.20.10/handoff.md","content":"## Task goal\nIndependently verify four small defect fixes in one commit, 65c37f2 (pre-build base 2c839cf). Tickets: .sdlc/.0259-fanout-gate-preflight, .sdlc/.0260-solo-session-limit-resume, .sdlc/.0262-close-citation-scan-gaps, .sdlc/.0273-codex-selftest-claude-path (read each handoff.md). Each regression test must fail without its fix and pass with it.\n\n## Step 1: Verify the four fixes\nlevel: L3\n\n### Do\n- T-0259 (scripts/fanout.py): an uncommitted handoff refusal now names the force-add of the ignored path; a plan whose start commit tracks package.json and whose gates never install prints a `note:` naming `npm ci`; a red gate in a worktree with package.json and no node_modules appends a hint. Test: fanout selftest case 20. Docs: docs/maintenance/sdlc-internals.md.\n- T-0260 (scripts/run.sh, scripts/solo_run.py): a failed run whose log shows 429 or a session limit writes `<role>-<level>.limit` and prints `run.sh: session limit: resume with: ...` (exit stays 1); solo_run.py writes `solo.limit` and prints a resume hint. Tests: run-selftest.sh case `session limit` and solo_run.py selftest.\n- T-0262 (scripts/tickets.py): `outside_refs` also scans the ticket root with ignore rules off so citations under a gitignored `.sdlc` are found, refused, and rewritable; `--force` prints `left refs to ...`. Test: tickets.py selftest `(u) refs` cases.\n- T-0273 (scripts/codex-selftest.py): `test_fanout_uses_codex` now checks argv (role script, and not the claude CLI) instead of a `claude` substring, so it passes when the repo path contains `claude`. This worktree lives under `.claude/worktrees`, which is the repro.\nTo show red before, work in a throwaway worktree under `$SDLC_TMP_WORKTREES` at HEAD, revert only the non-test hunks of each fix there (the `deps_note` call, the red-gate hint and the force-add wording in fanout.py; the `limit_marker` function body in run.sh and the `limit_hint` call in solo_run.py; the ignore-off scan block in `outside_refs`), run the matching selftest, and say what you did. For T-0273 run the OLD test body from base 2c839cf in this path and note that it fails.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/fanout.py selftest`\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/tickets.py selftest`\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/solo_run.py selftest`\n- `bash plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/run-selftest.sh`\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/codex-selftest.py CodexTests.test_fanout_uses_codex`\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/check.py`\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/codex_roles.py generate --check`\n- `python3 scripts/check-packaging.py`\n- Each of the four regression tests goes red with its fix reverted (observed, not read).\n\n## Builder note\nThe builder (Sonnet) saw red then green for each. Treat that as an unverified claim.\n","numLines":27,"startLine":1,"totalLines":27}}}
