{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016BmQ6UJb38eGKyaEK3Ayq3","type":"tool_result","content":"=================== 0259-fanout-gate-preflight ===================\n---\nid: T-0259\ntitle: \"fanout needs committed handoffs and node_modules in the gate worktree\"\ntype: chore           # feature | bug | chore | spike | idea\nstatus: proposed     # proposed | ready | blocked | done | dropped (build progress lives in /board)\nsize: S              # S | M | L | XL\npriority: P2         # P1 | P2 | P3\ndepends: []          # T-NNNN, file:<path>, cap:<name>; e.g. [T-0002]\ncreated: 2026-10-05\nrouter: .sdlc/AGENTS.md  # how to claim and close this ticket\n---\n\n## Goal\nDocument, or check up front with a clear message, what the fanout gate worktree needs.\n\n## Context\nfanout needs handoffs committed because `.sdlc` is gitignored. Its gate runs in a fresh worktree without `node_modules`; a `node_modules` symlink makes `build-editor-demo --check` fail. Evidence: maison `.worktrees/fanout/logs/gate-a-T-0066-1-a1.log` (`marked/package.json` ENOENT).\nScope: docs or a preflight message only. No fix of the gate itself.\n\n## Constraints\nNo push, tag, version bump, or publish. No em dashes.\n\n=================== 0260-solo-session-limit-resume ===================\n---\nid: T-0260\ntitle: \"Solo long commands capped at 30 min and session-limit stops leave no resume\"\ntype: bug             # feature | bug | chore | spike | idea\nstatus: proposed     # proposed | ready | blocked | done | dropped (build progress lives in /board)\nsize: M              # S | M | L | XL\npriority: P2         # P1 | P2 | P3\ndepends: []          # T-NNNN, file:<path>, cap:<name>; e.g. [T-0002]\ncreated: 2026-10-05\nrouter: .sdlc/AGENTS.md  # how to claim and close this ticket\n---\n\n## Goal\nA solo stopped by the 30 minute background cap or a session limit leaves a resume marker the conductor can act on.\n\n## Context\nTwo reports. 1) A solo's long foreground command is backgrounded by Claude Code and capped at 30 min regardless of the Bash timeout. 2) Session-limit stops leave `driver failed rc=1` with only a WIP commit and no resume; `run.sh` on a 429 session limit exits 1 with no resume marker.\nScope: file and design the marker and the guidance. No fix in this ticket's filing.\n\n## Constraints\nNo push, tag, version bump, or publish. No em dashes.\n\n=================== 0262-close-citation-scan-gaps ===================\n---\nid: T-0262\ntitle: \"tickets.py close needs --force on tracked citations and cannot see .sdlc citations\"\ntype: bug             # feature | bug | chore | spike | idea\nstatus: proposed     # proposed | ready | blocked | done | dropped (build progress lives in /board)\nsize: M              # S | M | L | XL\npriority: P2         # P1 | P2 | P3\ndepends: []          # T-NNNN, file:<path>, cap:<name>; e.g. [T-0002]\ncreated: 2026-10-05\nrouter: .sdlc/AGENTS.md  # how to claim and close this ticket\n---\n\n## Goal\n`tickets.py close` explains citation refusals better and sees `.sdlc` citations.\n\n## Context\nTwo gaps. 1) close refuses when tracked files cite the folder and needs `--force`. 2) The citation scan cannot see citations under `.sdlc`, so 14 links broke silently on a close. Evidence: conductor report, 0.20.8 field use.\nRead the ticket skill's close and `--rewrite-refs` text before editing.\n\n## Constraints\nNo push, tag, version bump, or publish. No em dashes.\n\n=================== 0273-codex-selftest-claude-path ===================\n---\nid: T-0273\ntitle: \"codex-selftest fanout test fails when repo path contains claude\"\ntype: bug             # feature | bug | chore | spike | idea\nstatus: proposed     # proposed | ready | blocked | done | dropped (build progress lives in /board)\nsize: S              # S | M | L | XL\npriority: P2         # P1 | P2 | P3\ndepends: []          # T-NNNN, file:<path>, cap:<name>; e.g. [T-0002]\ncreated: 2026-10-05\nrouter: .sdlc/AGENTS.md  # how to claim and close this ticket\n---\n\n## Goal\nThe bug is fixed and a test that failed before the fix passes after it.\n\n## Repro\nRun `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/codex-selftest.py CodexTests.test_fanout_uses_codex` from a checkout whose path contains `claude` (a worktree under `.claude/worktrees`).\n\n## Expected\nThe test passes: it checks that the Codex driver runs `codex_exec.py`, not the `claude` CLI.\n\n## Actual\n`AssertionError: 'claude' unexpectedly found in \"/.../.claude/worktrees/.../codex_exec.py conductor L1 ...\"`; the test searched the whole command string for `claude`, so the repo path failed it.\n\n## Context\ncodex-selftest.py `test_fanout_uses_codex`. Cause: a substring check on the command text instead of the argv role or backend.\n\n## Constraints\nThe failing test lands with the fix. No push, tag, version bump, or publish. No em dashes.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d37f6391-7843-414c-9b5f-3ff80d3a3d36","uuid":"e811e6b6-54e6-42a9-9f90-0ef7039b2af3","timestamp":"2026-10-05T23:26:58.228Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=================== 0259-fanout-gate-preflight ===================\n---\nid: T-0259\ntitle: \"fanout needs committed handoffs and node_modules in the gate worktree\"\ntype: chore           # feature | bug | chore | spike | idea\nstatus: proposed     # proposed | ready | blocked | done | dropped (build progress lives in /board)\nsize: S              # S | M | L | XL\npriority: P2         # P1 | P2 | P3\ndepends: []          # T-NNNN, file:<path>, cap:<name>; e.g. [T-0002]\ncreated: 2026-10-05\nrouter: .sdlc/AGENTS.md  # how to claim and close this ticket\n---\n\n## Goal\nDocument, or check up front with a clear message, what the fanout gate worktree needs.\n\n## Context\nfanout needs handoffs committed because `.sdlc` is gitignored. Its gate runs in a fresh worktree without `node_modules`; a `node_modules` symlink makes `build-editor-demo --check` fail. Evidence: maison `.worktrees/fanout/logs/gate-a-T-